1
00:00:10,677 --> 00:00:12,095
<i>Hello, everyone.</i>

2
00:00:12,178 --> 00:00:15,098
<i>It's the 2014 SNT National Track</i>
<i>and Field Meet.</i>

3
00:00:15,181 --> 00:00:17,767
<i>I'm Kim Seong-bae, your commentator.</i>

4
00:00:17,851 --> 00:00:22,313
<i>Finally, it's time for</i>
<i>the middle school girls' 200-meter final.</i>

5
00:00:22,397 --> 00:00:25,358
<i>Eight athletes are preparing to start.</i>

6
00:00:25,442 --> 00:00:26,276
<i>In lane eight</i>

7
00:00:26,359 --> 00:00:29,362
<i>stands frontrunner Byeon Ji-yoon</i>
<i>from Cheolma Girls' Middle School.</i>

8
00:00:29,446 --> 00:00:30,822
- On your marks!
<i>- Indeed.</i>

9
00:00:30,905 --> 00:00:33,658
<i>In terms of skill,</i>
<i>her start and early sprint are unmatched.</i>

10
00:00:33,742 --> 00:00:37,037
<i>But a poor semi-final run</i>
<i>puts her in lane eight today.</i>

11
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:41,082
<i>I heard Byeon Ji-yoon has an odd jinx.</i>

12
00:00:41,166 --> 00:00:44,878
<i>Yes. She somehow falls short</i>
<i>when she's in lane eight every time.</i>

13
00:00:44,961 --> 00:00:48,339
<i>Now, despite that,</i>
<i>Byeon Ji-yoon starts in lane eight.</i>

14
00:00:48,423 --> 00:00:51,509
<i>How will she perform in the finals?</i>

15
00:00:52,427 --> 00:00:55,472
<i>And the race starts</i>
<i>with the sound of the pistol.</i>

16
00:00:55,555 --> 00:00:58,266
<i>As expected, Byeon picks up speed</i>
<i>with an early sprint.</i>

17
00:00:58,349 --> 00:01:03,605
- <i>Can she finish strong? We'll have to see.</i>
- Byeon Ji-yoon, run! Run faster!

18
00:01:03,688 --> 00:01:07,192
Why rush at the start
if you only falter at the end, you idiot?

19
00:01:07,275 --> 00:01:10,570
Faster! Run faster! Run faster!
I said faster!

20
00:01:11,529 --> 00:01:12,697
<i>Are they gaining on me?</i>

21
00:01:12,781 --> 00:01:15,325
<i>What if I don't win? Are they on my heels?</i>

22
00:01:15,408 --> 00:01:16,951
<i>Stop thinking about trivial things.</i>

23
00:01:17,035 --> 00:01:18,953
<i>Don't think about anything else.</i>

24
00:01:19,037 --> 00:01:20,163
<i>Focus!</i>

25
00:01:20,246 --> 00:01:21,372
<i>You need to focus.</i>

26
00:01:21,456 --> 00:01:22,582
<i>Just look ahead and run.</i>

27
00:01:23,792 --> 00:01:24,834
<i>Eyes ahead. Run.</i>

28
00:01:24,918 --> 00:01:25,919
<i>Wait a minute.</i>

29
00:01:27,003 --> 00:01:28,338
<i>Something feels off.</i>

30
00:01:48,983 --> 00:01:51,444
<i>Hey! Get up!</i>

31
00:01:52,070 --> 00:01:53,363
<i>Get the hell up!</i>

32
00:02:06,835 --> 00:02:08,837
Goddamn it. Seriously.

33
00:02:09,504 --> 00:02:10,547
YOU HAVE NOT BEEN
SELECTED FOR THE JOB

34
00:02:10,672 --> 00:02:12,090
Like I care. Damn it.

35
00:02:12,173 --> 00:02:13,842
IF YOU CAN'T REACH ME,
GO TO SPIDER STAFFING AGEN CY

36
00:03:09,230 --> 00:03:12,901
DEAD-END JOB

37
00:03:14,068 --> 00:03:17,030
EPISODE 4
MIDNIGHT FANTASY CINEMA

38
00:03:17,989 --> 00:03:19,949
CHEOLMA GIRLS' MIDDLE SCHOOL BULLDOZER

39
00:03:20,033 --> 00:03:21,117
Okay.

40
00:03:25,079 --> 00:03:25,914
<i>Defeat.</i>

41
00:03:26,414 --> 00:03:27,624
Damn it!

42
00:03:33,296 --> 00:03:34,881
What should I eat?

43
00:03:42,764 --> 00:03:45,475
BYEON HYEOK-JUN: IF YOU CAN'T REACH ME,
GO TO SPIDER STAFFING AGEN CY

44
00:03:45,642 --> 00:03:47,185
<i>"Spider Staffing Agency"?</i>

45
00:03:52,523 --> 00:03:54,817
BYEON HYEOK-JUN

46
00:03:58,446 --> 00:04:01,241
<i>The number you have dialed is currently</i>…

47
00:04:01,324 --> 00:04:02,533
What's with this fool?

48
00:04:07,372 --> 00:04:08,790
Spider Staffing Agency…

49
00:04:09,290 --> 00:04:10,583
SPIDER STAFFING AGENCY

50
00:04:10,708 --> 00:04:14,712
He could've left an address.
There's more than one staffing agency.

51
00:04:16,798 --> 00:04:17,882
There's only one.

52
00:04:18,466 --> 00:04:23,263
SPIDER STAFFING AGENCY

53
00:04:28,685 --> 00:04:31,521
SPIDER STAFFING AGENCY

54
00:04:32,105 --> 00:04:33,564
Now this is suspicious.

55
00:04:35,149 --> 00:04:37,402
Wouldn’t "Ant" be more fitting?

56
00:04:52,542 --> 00:04:53,835
Hello.

57
00:04:53,918 --> 00:04:55,378
- Welcome.
- Thanks.

58
00:04:55,878 --> 00:04:57,505
Are you here for a job?

59
00:04:59,299 --> 00:05:01,342
Well…

60
00:05:01,426 --> 00:05:02,468
Just a moment.

61
00:05:02,969 --> 00:05:04,095
This is Byeon Hyeok-jun.

62
00:05:04,721 --> 00:05:08,641
He's a bit taller than me,
looks a bit dopey, and is 30 years old.

63
00:05:08,725 --> 00:05:10,393
Did he work here, by any chance?

64
00:05:12,603 --> 00:05:14,022
Mr. Hyeok-jun?

65
00:05:14,105 --> 00:05:15,064
Yes.

66
00:05:16,357 --> 00:05:17,191
Older sister?

67
00:05:20,653 --> 00:05:22,280
- Younger, actually.
- I see.

68
00:05:24,032 --> 00:05:26,576
Did Mr. Hyeok-jun
suggest this place to you?

69
00:05:28,202 --> 00:05:31,247
"If you can't reach me,
go to Spider Staffing Agency."

70
00:05:31,331 --> 00:05:33,541
Isn't this the Spider Staffing Agency?

71
00:05:34,167 --> 00:05:37,086
He sent me this,
and I haven't heard from him since.

72
00:05:38,796 --> 00:05:41,758
Well, we don't know
what's going on either.

73
00:05:41,841 --> 00:05:45,595
How does a staffing agency not know?
Where did he go to work?

74
00:05:47,889 --> 00:05:50,266
I'm sorry, but we can't tell you that.

75
00:05:51,434 --> 00:05:54,562
We must protect the privacy
of both the worker and the client.

76
00:05:58,399 --> 00:06:00,651
Do you know that sounds really suspicious?

77
00:06:00,735 --> 00:06:02,737
Have you been to the police?

78
00:06:03,237 --> 00:06:04,072
What?

79
00:06:04,155 --> 00:06:07,200
If you can't reach a family member,
you should report them missing.

80
00:06:07,784 --> 00:06:10,411
Although it seems
Mr. Hyeok-jun wanted you, Ms. Ji-yoon,

81
00:06:10,495 --> 00:06:13,873
to come here instead of going
to the police, for some reason.

82
00:06:14,624 --> 00:06:15,500
Wait, hold on.

83
00:06:15,583 --> 00:06:17,835
How did you know my name?

84
00:06:17,919 --> 00:06:19,295
Did he tell you about me?

85
00:06:27,387 --> 00:06:28,971
Seriously, he doesn't answer.

86
00:06:29,055 --> 00:06:30,681
So frustrating, damn it.

87
00:06:31,599 --> 00:06:33,142
Okay.

88
00:06:33,226 --> 00:06:34,685
I can take one, right?

89
00:06:34,769 --> 00:06:37,772
Make sure to answer
when the police call you.

90
00:06:38,856 --> 00:06:40,733
Give me a call if you need a job.

91
00:06:41,943 --> 00:06:44,237
You'd be better at this
than your little brother.

92
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:46,030
I'm younger!

93
00:06:58,876 --> 00:07:01,712
<i>I'm afraid this isn't enough</i>
<i>to report him missing.</i>

94
00:07:02,213 --> 00:07:04,966
<i>Most of these cases</i>
<i>are usually just runaways and pranks.</i>

95
00:07:46,757 --> 00:07:47,717
Excuse me.

96
00:07:49,343 --> 00:07:52,305
I know you've been following me.
Don't play dumb.

97
00:07:56,767 --> 00:07:58,561
You're quick to notice things.

98
00:07:59,645 --> 00:08:00,813
Unlike your older brother.

99
00:08:05,401 --> 00:08:06,694
Do you know my brother?

100
00:08:06,777 --> 00:08:07,695
Of course.

101
00:08:08,196 --> 00:08:09,489
Mr. Byeon Hyeok-jun.

102
00:08:15,286 --> 00:08:17,538
Today is such a weird day, seriously.

103
00:08:19,248 --> 00:08:20,917
Why don't we have a chat?

104
00:08:21,542 --> 00:08:23,920
I think I might be able to help you.

105
00:08:25,630 --> 00:08:27,006
WORKERS' COMPENSATION UNION
EUM YEON-JOO

106
00:08:27,131 --> 00:08:28,633
"Accident investigator"?

107
00:08:37,183 --> 00:08:41,479
What exactly are you saying happened
to Byeon Hyeok-jun?

108
00:08:42,146 --> 00:08:43,314
Before that,

109
00:08:44,941 --> 00:08:48,736
let's deal with
that spying, white-robed ghost behind us.

110
00:08:56,077 --> 00:08:57,453
That's an apron.

111
00:08:58,204 --> 00:09:01,249
Then what about that child
staring at us from the window?

112
00:09:10,466 --> 00:09:12,802
You really are different
from your brother.

113
00:09:13,344 --> 00:09:14,303
Don't you get scared?

114
00:09:14,887 --> 00:09:16,222
Of course I get scared.

115
00:09:17,014 --> 00:09:18,349
I get scared easily.

116
00:09:19,183 --> 00:09:22,603
I get scared when my only pair of nylons
is ruined before a job interview.

117
00:09:22,687 --> 00:09:26,774
And when my budget's tight for the month
and I get a friend's wedding invitation.

118
00:09:26,857 --> 00:09:29,026
When I can't split the fee
for my Netflix account.

119
00:09:29,110 --> 00:09:32,029
Taxi fares, hospital bills, you name it.
They all scare me.

120
00:09:33,656 --> 00:09:36,576
So I couldn't care less
about ghosts like that.

121
00:09:38,369 --> 00:09:41,372
So forget about ghosts.
Let's talk about Byeon Hyeok-jun.

122
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:44,792
If I'm right,

123
00:09:45,293 --> 00:09:48,212
Mr. Hyeok-jun is at the threshold
of the other world.

124
00:09:52,341 --> 00:09:54,969
I got a C in Korean.

125
00:09:55,636 --> 00:09:58,180
So cut the poetic talk
and just give me the address

126
00:09:58,264 --> 00:09:59,640
so I can go there.

127
00:10:00,141 --> 00:10:02,268
I was being literal, not poetic.

128
00:10:02,768 --> 00:10:03,936
The other world.

129
00:10:07,940 --> 00:10:09,275
So are you saying

130
00:10:09,942 --> 00:10:12,486
that I can find Byeon Hyeok-jun or not?

131
00:10:12,570 --> 00:10:13,738
You probably can.

132
00:10:14,363 --> 00:10:18,784
If you go to work part-time.
It's connected to the other world.

133
00:10:21,996 --> 00:10:25,499
Seriously, what the hell am I doing here?

134
00:10:26,959 --> 00:10:29,920
Good luck with the part-time job.
I'll be leaving now.

135
00:10:31,756 --> 00:10:33,424
Don't you want to find your brother?

136
00:10:37,219 --> 00:10:39,055
I know it's hard to believe.

137
00:10:41,307 --> 00:10:43,476
But if you really want
to find your brother,

138
00:10:44,935 --> 00:10:46,562
I suggest you do as I say.

139
00:10:49,190 --> 00:10:54,695
BYEON HYEOK-JUN: IF YOU CAN'T REACH ME,
GO TO SPIDER STAFFING AGEN CY

140
00:11:00,409 --> 00:11:01,327
Hey, listen.

141
00:11:01,952 --> 00:11:03,913
Say there's a part-time job

142
00:11:03,996 --> 00:11:07,917
that pays dozens,
hundreds of times the minimum wage.

143
00:11:09,335 --> 00:11:10,795
But the problem is…

144
00:11:13,381 --> 00:11:16,008
all kinds of fucked-up shit
keeps coming at you.

145
00:11:16,092 --> 00:11:19,136
Like ghosts, monsters, bugs, like--

146
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:20,054
I'd do it.

147
00:11:20,137 --> 00:11:21,764
I'd do it a hundred times.

148
00:11:22,473 --> 00:11:25,643
At least let me finish talking
before you answer. Seriously…

149
00:11:25,726 --> 00:11:28,646
I'm more scared of being broke
than I am of ghosts.

150
00:11:34,985 --> 00:11:40,533
SPIDER STAFFING AGENCY

151
00:11:51,794 --> 00:11:53,629
<i>Yes, Spider Staffing Agency.</i>

152
00:11:56,215 --> 00:11:57,425
<i>How can I help you?</i>

153
00:11:58,092 --> 00:11:59,802
I'd like a job.

154
00:12:06,559 --> 00:12:09,270
NEW WORLD CINEMA, PART-TIME JOB
50 TIMES THE DAILY WAGE, 11 P.M. - 5 A.M.

155
00:12:09,353 --> 00:12:11,522
WHY AREN'T YOU ANSWERING?
GOING TO SPIDER STAFFING AGENCY

156
00:12:11,605 --> 00:12:13,190
REPORTED YOU MISSING
MET EUM YEON-JOO

157
00:12:13,274 --> 00:12:16,110
Seriously, Byeon Hyeok-jun.
You're such a damn pain in the ass.

158
00:12:16,193 --> 00:12:17,486
AT A WEIRD PART-TIME JOB TO FIND YOU

159
00:12:24,285 --> 00:12:26,704
Like people would come
to a place like this.

160
00:12:33,377 --> 00:12:34,879
<i>If you want to find your brother,</i>

161
00:12:34,962 --> 00:12:37,590
<i>you need to find the passage</i>
<i>to the other world first.</i>

162
00:12:38,466 --> 00:12:41,343
<i>To do that, first,</i>
<i>pretend you're working a part-time job.</i>

163
00:12:41,844 --> 00:12:45,473
<i>It could get dangerous</i>
<i>if they find out you're up to something.</i>

164
00:12:51,896 --> 00:12:54,190
Hi. You must be the part-timer.

165
00:12:54,690 --> 00:12:56,484
Yes, hello.

166
00:12:56,984 --> 00:12:58,778
You have pretty eyes.

167
00:13:00,404 --> 00:13:01,697
I'm Byeon Ji-yoon.

168
00:13:02,782 --> 00:13:03,699
Which agency?

169
00:13:03,783 --> 00:13:05,075
Spider Staffing Agency.

170
00:13:07,203 --> 00:13:09,121
- So you're from Spider.
- Yes.

171
00:13:12,166 --> 00:13:13,292
You're from Spider.

172
00:13:13,375 --> 00:13:16,003
Do you have any movie theater experience?

173
00:13:17,004 --> 00:13:19,465
Once, for three months
during school break.

174
00:13:19,548 --> 00:13:22,092
- Three months. Then you must be good.
- Yes.

175
00:13:24,637 --> 00:13:26,764
That's nice.

176
00:13:32,978 --> 00:13:35,231
- You're a smoker, aren't you?
- Yes.

177
00:13:35,773 --> 00:13:36,649
That's good.

178
00:13:37,566 --> 00:13:41,237
<i>Second, there will be an obstacle</i>
<i>guarding the passage.</i>

179
00:13:42,613 --> 00:13:44,573
<i>I don't know what form they'll take.</i>

180
00:13:45,074 --> 00:13:45,950
<i>But…</i>

181
00:13:48,285 --> 00:13:51,413
you'll feel like
you shouldn't be alone with them.

182
00:13:53,082 --> 00:13:54,750
<i>If you find that person…</i>

183
00:13:58,963 --> 00:14:01,340
tase them, because they're an obstacle.

184
00:14:09,640 --> 00:14:11,767
Welcome to New World Cinema.

185
00:14:13,519 --> 00:14:14,562
Let's get to work.

186
00:14:22,987 --> 00:14:24,697
Enjoy the movie.

187
00:14:37,918 --> 00:14:39,044
<i>Third…</i>

188
00:14:40,754 --> 00:14:42,423
<i>you don't see anything right now,</i>

189
00:14:43,424 --> 00:14:45,926
but you'll be able
to see letters in the dark.

190
00:14:50,139 --> 00:14:52,516
<i>Look for the place where you're working.</i>

191
00:14:52,641 --> 00:14:54,143
INTERNET CAFÉ, POWER OUTLET,
COVENIENCE STORE, FRIDGE…

192
00:14:54,226 --> 00:14:57,313
The word next to it
is the door to the other world.

193
00:14:57,396 --> 00:14:58,606
PUB, FRYER, MILK DELIVERY, 505…

194
00:14:58,731 --> 00:15:02,276
<i>Remove the obstacle and cross the passage.</i>
<i>You'll find your brother there.</i>

195
00:15:02,359 --> 00:15:03,235
MOVIE THEATER, SCREEN 7

196
00:15:05,613 --> 00:15:07,489
"Screen 7"?

197
00:15:37,269 --> 00:15:39,897
Screen 6 has a total of eight people.

198
00:15:40,856 --> 00:15:43,442
<i>What? But we only sold seven tickets.</i>

199
00:15:44,693 --> 00:15:45,527
What?

200
00:15:46,111 --> 00:15:47,988
I have eight checked tickets here.

201
00:15:49,031 --> 00:15:51,533
<i>That's weird.</i>
<i>We clearly sold seven tickets.</i>

202
00:15:52,034 --> 00:15:53,285
<i>Then is the extra person</i>

203
00:15:54,703 --> 00:15:55,663
<i>a ghost?</i>

204
00:15:57,164 --> 00:15:59,333
<i>I'm just kidding. Did I scare you?</i>

205
00:15:59,416 --> 00:16:02,252
- <i>Lead the audience out and clean Screen 5.</i>
- Okay.

206
00:16:04,380 --> 00:16:06,715
Jerk. Joking around and shit.

207
00:16:10,511 --> 00:16:13,013
Were everyone’s jaws too busy
to hold the popcorn in?

208
00:16:26,443 --> 00:16:29,905
Excuse me, you can leave now.
There's no post-credits scene.

209
00:16:32,116 --> 00:16:34,118
There's no post-credits scene, sir.

210
00:16:47,214 --> 00:16:48,507
Damn it.

211
00:16:48,590 --> 00:16:52,469
What the hell is this?
Did they eat <i>tanghulu </i>or something?

212
00:16:57,975 --> 00:17:00,769
(AD) LOOKING FOR SOMEONE
TO SHARE A HOT, SIZZLING NIGHT

213
00:17:00,853 --> 00:17:02,563
A hot night, my ass.

214
00:17:05,983 --> 00:17:07,192
You scared me.

215
00:17:12,031 --> 00:17:13,824
Mister, do you need something?

216
00:17:19,079 --> 00:17:22,249
Come on, really?
Who still does the trench coat flash?

217
00:17:25,919 --> 00:17:27,337
Come here, you bastard.

218
00:17:39,558 --> 00:17:40,392
What the hell?

219
00:17:40,893 --> 00:17:42,019
How'd he do that?

220
00:17:43,896 --> 00:17:45,898
There are all kinds of perverts out there.

221
00:17:52,196 --> 00:17:53,197
Jji-yoon.

222
00:17:54,281 --> 00:17:55,407
What are those?

223
00:17:56,241 --> 00:17:59,953
Lost items some perv bastard left behind.
Not sure if they'll be claimed.

224
00:18:00,037 --> 00:18:01,872
Oh, the flasher.

225
00:18:02,498 --> 00:18:07,503
But maybe we can't say for sure
because no one has actually seen him.

226
00:18:09,296 --> 00:18:11,507
Why can't we? A pervert is a pervert.

227
00:18:12,007 --> 00:18:14,051
He seemed to be a repeat offender too.

228
00:18:14,134 --> 00:18:16,470
The previous part-timers said otherwise.

229
00:18:17,054 --> 00:18:18,222
They said it was a ghost.

230
00:18:20,057 --> 00:18:22,601
Come on, a ghost?
I don't believe in that stuff.

231
00:18:22,684 --> 00:18:23,936
You're gutsy, aren't you?

232
00:18:25,604 --> 00:18:26,730
Check.

233
00:18:28,023 --> 00:18:29,108
Keep up the good work.

234
00:18:33,320 --> 00:18:34,196
Damn it.

235
00:18:45,916 --> 00:18:49,294
What kind of ghost
has more clothes than I do?

236
00:18:59,972 --> 00:19:03,475
LOST AND FOUND

237
00:19:10,023 --> 00:19:11,692
Is this broken or something?

238
00:19:11,775 --> 00:19:12,693
Knock, knock.

239
00:19:13,861 --> 00:19:14,945
Excuse me.

240
00:19:15,946 --> 00:19:17,823
Can I help you with something?

241
00:19:18,907 --> 00:19:19,950
I just

242
00:19:20,784 --> 00:19:22,077
came out of Screen 6.

243
00:19:23,370 --> 00:19:27,374
Why are you showing a CinemaScope movie
on a VistaVision screen?

244
00:19:27,958 --> 00:19:31,420
You should at least mask the letterbox,
but you didn't even do that.

245
00:19:32,129 --> 00:19:32,963
Sorry?

246
00:19:33,046 --> 00:19:35,090
The screen is blurry
on the top and bottom.

247
00:19:37,301 --> 00:19:38,343
It ruins the immersion.

248
00:19:41,889 --> 00:19:44,892
I'm sorry. I don't really watch movies.

249
00:19:48,937 --> 00:19:50,689
You don't watch movies?

250
00:19:50,772 --> 00:19:51,648
No.

251
00:19:56,695 --> 00:19:58,113
Are you okay? What's wrong?

252
00:20:02,993 --> 00:20:04,411
The movie <i>Parasite</i>

253
00:20:04,494 --> 00:20:08,665
won four Oscars, including Best Picture,
at the 92nd Academy Awards in 2020.

254
00:20:08,749 --> 00:20:10,459
The film's director, Bong Joon Ho,

255
00:20:10,542 --> 00:20:14,421
is the father of actor Bong Tae-gyu
from the movie <i>Family Ties. </i>True or false?

256
00:20:15,130 --> 00:20:16,048
Sorry?

257
00:20:16,131 --> 00:20:17,174
True or false?

258
00:20:19,426 --> 00:20:20,969
- True?
- The answer is false.

259
00:20:21,637 --> 00:20:22,554
Lee Dong-jin,

260
00:20:22,638 --> 00:20:24,473
Korea's most recognized film critic

261
00:20:24,556 --> 00:20:29,353
and an icon in the field,
wears red glasses. True or false?

262
00:20:29,436 --> 00:20:30,395
False.

263
00:20:30,479 --> 00:20:31,480
The answer is true.

264
00:20:31,563 --> 00:20:34,233
Damn it. Who the hell wears red glasses?

265
00:20:34,316 --> 00:20:36,151
You really don't know anything.

266
00:20:37,569 --> 00:20:40,197
Last chance.
What is the title of this movie?

267
00:20:45,244 --> 00:20:47,621
Umbrella. Rain.

268
00:20:49,331 --> 00:20:50,791
Smile. Smile?

269
00:20:51,875 --> 00:20:52,709
Do it again.

270
00:20:56,755 --> 00:20:58,090
You run over.

271
00:20:59,758 --> 00:21:01,969
Umbrella. Smile.

272
00:21:02,052 --> 00:21:03,387
It's raining. Rain…

273
00:21:03,887 --> 00:21:04,972
You use an umbrella

274
00:21:05,472 --> 00:21:06,515
and smile.

275
00:21:07,266 --> 00:21:08,100
Could it be…

276
00:21:13,522 --> 00:21:14,356
It can't be.

277
00:21:15,274 --> 00:21:16,275
Is it

278
00:21:17,234 --> 00:21:18,193
<i>Romance of Their Own</i>?

279
00:21:23,282 --> 00:21:24,116
What the…

280
00:21:25,242 --> 00:21:26,243
You do watch movies.

281
00:21:27,286 --> 00:21:28,120
See you again.

282
00:21:28,203 --> 00:21:29,329
I got it right?

283
00:21:31,957 --> 00:21:32,916
Is he a weirdo?

284
00:21:33,667 --> 00:21:34,626
<i>Jji-yoon.</i>

285
00:21:35,127 --> 00:21:36,628
<i>Who were you talking to just now?</i>

286
00:21:37,129 --> 00:21:39,923
Some crazy guy just randomly quizzed me.
What's with him?

287
00:21:40,424 --> 00:21:42,092
<i>Oh, Movie Quiz?</i>

288
00:21:42,175 --> 00:21:44,303
<i>That punk came again. Did anything happen?</i>

289
00:21:44,386 --> 00:21:45,762
He just left.

290
00:21:46,346 --> 00:21:47,848
<i>You were lucky.</i>

291
00:21:48,348 --> 00:21:50,434
<i>I heard if you miss</i>
<i>three questions in a row,</i>

292
00:21:50,517 --> 00:21:54,563
<i>he stabs you in the mouth with an awl.</i>
<i>Or was it that he rips your mouth open?</i>

293
00:21:54,646 --> 00:21:57,274
<i>Anyway, he jabs you or something.</i>

294
00:21:57,357 --> 00:21:58,942
<i>You did well.</i>

295
00:22:01,486 --> 00:22:04,197
<i>Jji-yoon, is seating done in Screen 7?</i>

296
00:22:04,865 --> 00:22:07,409
Screen 7 is empty.
No need to play the movie.

297
00:22:07,993 --> 00:22:09,995
<i>What? Isn't there one person?</i>

298
00:22:10,078 --> 00:22:12,372
Come on. Stop messing with me.

299
00:22:12,914 --> 00:22:13,749
<i>What do you mean?</i>

300
00:22:13,832 --> 00:22:16,209
<i>The projectionist said</i>
<i>there's one person in Screen 7.</i>

301
00:22:18,503 --> 00:22:19,338
What?

302
00:22:20,130 --> 00:22:22,341
<i>Maybe someone went into the wrong theater.</i>

303
00:22:22,424 --> 00:22:23,842
<i>Go check it out, Ji-yoon.</i>

304
00:22:30,766 --> 00:22:31,892
Screen 7.

305
00:22:36,021 --> 00:22:38,357
<i>Look for the place where you're working.</i>

306
00:22:39,358 --> 00:22:41,943
<i>The word next to it</i>
<i>is the door to the other world.</i>

307
00:22:42,027 --> 00:22:43,278
MOVIE THEATER SCREEN 7

308
00:22:43,403 --> 00:22:46,823
<i>Remove the obstacle and cross the passage.</i>
<i>You'll find your brother there.</i>

309
00:23:19,564 --> 00:23:20,440
Excuse me?

310
00:23:32,202 --> 00:23:33,453
The obstacle.

311
00:23:46,007 --> 00:23:46,883
Ma'am?

312
00:23:47,968 --> 00:23:50,053
May I check your ticket, please?

313
00:23:58,645 --> 00:24:03,150
<i>Finally, it's time for the middle</i>
<i>school girls' 200-meter final.</i>

314
00:24:03,233 --> 00:24:06,236
<i>Eight athletes are preparing to start.</i>

315
00:24:06,319 --> 00:24:07,154
<i>In lane eight</i>

316
00:24:07,237 --> 00:24:10,240
<i>stands frontrunner Byeon Ji-yoon</i>
<i>from Cheolma Girls' Middle School.</i>

317
00:24:10,323 --> 00:24:13,660
- <i>In terms of skill, her start and early…</i>
- What is this? What's going on?

318
00:24:13,743 --> 00:24:15,245
Is anyone in the projection room?

319
00:24:15,328 --> 00:24:17,998
<i>- But a poor semi-final run</i>…
- What is this?

320
00:24:18,081 --> 00:24:21,084
<i>- I heard Byeon Ji-yoon has an odd jinx.</i>
- What are you doing?

321
00:24:22,627 --> 00:24:25,714
<i>- …falls short when she's in lane eight.</i>
<i>- Get set!</i>

322
00:24:26,214 --> 00:24:28,758
<i>And the race starts</i>
<i>with the sound of the pistol.</i>

323
00:24:28,842 --> 00:24:31,428
<i>…Byeon Ji-yoon picks up speed</i>
<i>with an early sprint.</i>

324
00:24:31,511 --> 00:24:35,182
- Why won't it open? Hey, let me out!
- <i>Can she finish strong? We'll have to see.</i>

325
00:24:48,945 --> 00:24:51,781
Please! Come on, open! Please!

326
00:25:04,961 --> 00:25:06,838
What? What is this?

327
00:25:18,183 --> 00:25:21,770
No, I need to wake up. Come on.

328
00:25:26,107 --> 00:25:27,400
Shit, screw it.

329
00:25:43,959 --> 00:25:46,002
Damn it! I need to wake up!

330
00:25:46,086 --> 00:25:47,546
How the hell do I wake up?

331
00:25:49,005 --> 00:25:49,839
Stay away!

332
00:25:49,923 --> 00:25:51,258
Oh please.

333
00:26:09,192 --> 00:26:11,361
Damn it.

334
00:26:11,903 --> 00:26:15,574
- <i>Byeon Ji-yoon!</i>
- Damn it.

335
00:26:15,657 --> 00:26:20,495
<i>Byeon Ji-yoon!</i>

336
00:26:21,246 --> 00:26:28,253
<i>Byeon Ji-yoon!</i>

337
00:26:28,795 --> 00:26:30,797
- Who is it? Is no one here?
- <i>Byeon Ji-yoon!</i>

338
00:26:30,880 --> 00:26:34,718
<i>Byeon Ji-yoon!</i>

339
00:26:34,801 --> 00:26:39,180
<i>Byeon Ji-yoon! Byeon Ji--</i>

340
00:26:51,693 --> 00:26:52,527
Ji-yoon.

341
00:26:57,407 --> 00:26:58,491
What's with the chair?

342
00:27:00,493 --> 00:27:01,536
Are you working out?

343
00:27:04,873 --> 00:27:09,502
No, damn it. The projection room
keeps playing something weird.

344
00:27:09,586 --> 00:27:11,963
I came to check, but no one's here.

345
00:27:13,006 --> 00:27:16,176
The projection room
isn't your responsibility. Go back down.

346
00:27:16,676 --> 00:27:20,347
But they keep playing something weird
in an empty theater.

347
00:27:20,889 --> 00:27:22,057
This…

348
00:27:23,016 --> 00:27:26,269
This machine does that sometimes.

349
00:27:28,772 --> 00:27:31,232
- Ji-yoon. Get a grip.
- Shit.

350
00:27:32,776 --> 00:27:36,154
You just need to kill time
and get through your shift.

351
00:27:36,905 --> 00:27:37,739
Right?

352
00:27:39,699 --> 00:27:40,700
So…

353
00:27:43,870 --> 00:27:45,955
- How about a smoke?
- Damn it.

354
00:27:46,039 --> 00:27:47,874
- Come on.
- Goddammit, seriously!

355
00:27:59,719 --> 00:28:00,970
What the hell?

356
00:28:06,893 --> 00:28:07,769
What the…

357
00:28:11,272 --> 00:28:12,315
No.

358
00:28:13,149 --> 00:28:15,151
It's not what you think. I can explain.

359
00:28:16,319 --> 00:28:17,153
Crazy bastard.

360
00:28:20,115 --> 00:28:22,117
- It's you, you bastard!
- What's me?

361
00:28:22,784 --> 00:28:23,952
You damn obstacle.

362
00:28:24,035 --> 00:28:25,328
It's not me! Let me--

363
00:28:54,274 --> 00:28:55,233
Hello?

364
00:28:56,109 --> 00:28:57,235
<i>Ms. Byeon Ji-yoon?</i>

365
00:28:58,319 --> 00:28:59,362
Spider Staffing Agency?

366
00:28:59,863 --> 00:29:02,699
<i>Why are you answering the phone?</i>
<i>Where's the manager?</i>

367
00:29:04,659 --> 00:29:07,078
I took care of the damn manager.

368
00:29:07,162 --> 00:29:10,749
I had a bad feeling about this bastard
from the beginning.

369
00:29:10,832 --> 00:29:13,168
<i>What are you talking about?</i>
<i>Why would you do that?</i>

370
00:29:14,544 --> 00:29:16,504
- <i>Where is the manager now?</i>
- He's…

371
00:29:17,005 --> 00:29:19,174
<i>Where is the manager now?</i>

372
00:29:22,343 --> 00:29:23,386
<i>Ms. Byeon Ji-yoon.</i>

373
00:29:23,887 --> 00:29:26,139
<i>What in the world are you doing there?</i>

374
00:29:26,639 --> 00:29:27,724
<i>Are you even listening?</i>

375
00:29:29,017 --> 00:29:30,477
<i>Don't make things worse.</i>

376
00:29:31,060 --> 00:29:34,314
<i>Don't do or mess with anything</i>
<i>until the end of your shift.</i>

377
00:29:36,399 --> 00:29:37,484
Screen.

378
00:29:38,067 --> 00:29:39,527
Obstacle.

379
00:29:50,330 --> 00:29:51,706
Damn it, this'll do.

380
00:30:14,771 --> 00:30:15,980
You piece of shit.

381
00:30:18,817 --> 00:30:20,819
It's you, isn't it? You bastard.

382
00:30:21,319 --> 00:30:22,904
Do you know who the hell I am?

383
00:30:22,987 --> 00:30:25,490
I'm the damn track athlete
from Cheolma Girls'…

384
00:30:50,515 --> 00:30:52,308
Damn it!

385
00:30:56,229 --> 00:30:58,565
You're dead, bastard.

386
00:31:02,527 --> 00:31:04,279
You lousy scumbag.

387
00:31:49,032 --> 00:31:50,617
Who said I can't finish strong?

388
00:31:51,784 --> 00:31:53,745
I'm fucking persistent, damn it.

389
00:32:02,545 --> 00:32:05,506
<i>After you eliminate the obstacle,</i>
<i>find the door.</i>

390
00:32:08,760 --> 00:32:11,346
Movie theater, Screen 7.

391
00:32:20,104 --> 00:32:21,856
What door is she talking about?

392
00:32:26,361 --> 00:32:27,487
A door handle?

393
00:32:53,930 --> 00:32:55,014
Byeon Hyeok-jun?

394
00:33:12,031 --> 00:33:13,199
What the fuck?

395
00:33:18,997 --> 00:33:20,748
Hold on.

396
00:33:22,250 --> 00:33:25,003
MISSED CALL
BYEON JI-YOON

397
00:33:25,086 --> 00:33:26,045
BYEON JI-YOON
WHERE ARE YOU?

398
00:33:29,215 --> 00:33:30,133
Oh thank God.

399
00:33:30,883 --> 00:33:33,136
WHY AREN'T YOU ANSWERING?
GOING TO SPIDER STAFFING AGENCY

400
00:33:36,472 --> 00:33:37,306
Hey.

401
00:33:38,057 --> 00:33:40,351
Ji-yoon, what the hell
are you talking about?

402
00:33:40,435 --> 00:33:42,145
Why would you work a part-time job?

403
00:33:42,270 --> 00:33:44,731
AT A WEIRD PART-TIME JOB TO FIND YOU

404
00:38:03,656 --> 00:38:07,076
Subtitle translation by: Yung Un Choi
